      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "questdb-questdb-datasource",
            "uid": "QuestDB"
          },
          "format": 1,
          "queryType": "sql",
          "meta": {},
          "rawSql": "SELECT 100 * cast(sum(case when segment = 'cel' then value end) AS DOUBLE)\n           / cast(sum(value) AS DOUBLE) AS \"CEL % of Consumption\"\nFROM cel_energy\nWHERE $__timeFilter(ts)\n  AND meter_id LIKE '%$meter_id'\n  AND direction = 'consumption'\n  AND segment in ('cel', 'grid')",
          "refId": "A",
          "selectedFormat": 1,
          "promqlOriginal": "(sum(increase(cel_energy_kwh{segment=\"cel\", direction=\"consumption\", meter_id=~\".*${meter_id}\"}[$__range])) / (sum(increase(cel_energy_kwh{segment=\"grid\", direction=\"consumption\", meter_id=~\".*${meter_id}\"}[$__range])) + sum(increase(cel_energy_kwh{segment=\"cel\", direction=\"consumption\", meter_id=~\".*${meter_id}\"}[$__range])))) * 100"
        }
      ],
      "title": "CEL % of Consumption",
      "type": "gauge",
      "description": "Ratio of summed kWh over the dashboard's time range. The PromQL original wrapped this in increase(...[$__range]), which treats a gauge as a counter: cel_energy_kwh is kWh-per-15-min-slot and falls as well as rises, so every decrease read as a counter reset and the ratio was computed from accumulated positive deltas rather than from the totals. sum(value) is what the panel title always claimed to show, so this port is a deliberate correction -- expect it to disagree with the VM gauge."
    },
