          "format": 0,
          "queryType": "sql",
          "meta": {},
          "rawSql": "SELECT ts AS time, cast(avg(slot_kwh) * 4 AS DOUBLE) AS \"Net Energy (positive = producing more)\"\nFROM (\n  SELECT ts, sum(case when direction = 'production' then value else value * -1 end) AS slot_kwh\n  FROM cel_energy\n  WHERE $__timeFilter(ts)\n    AND segment in ('cel', 'grid')\n    AND meter_id LIKE '%$meter_id'\n  SAMPLE BY 15m\n)\nSAMPLE BY $__sampleByInterval FILL(NULL)\nORDER BY time",
          "refId": "A",
          "selectedFormat": 0,
          "promqlOriginal": "((avg_over_time(sum(cel_energy_kwh{segment=\"grid\", direction=\"production\", meter_id=~\".*${meter_id}\"})[$__interval:15m]) + avg_over_time(sum(cel_energy_kwh{segment=\"cel\", direction=\"production\", meter_id=~\".*${meter_id}\"})[$__interval:15m])) - (avg_over_time(sum(cel_energy_kwh{segment=\"grid\", direction=\"consumption\", meter_id=~\".*${meter_id}\"})[$__interval:15m]) + avg_over_time(sum(cel_energy_kwh{segment=\"cel\", direction=\"consumption\", meter_id=~\".*${meter_id}\"})[$__interval:15m]))) * 4"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Energy Balance - ${meter_id}",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "interval": "15m",
      "description": "Net = production - consumption per 15-min slot, as kW. One signed sum rather than four averages: a slot with only consumption rows would make the production term NULL and blank the series. cast(... AS DOUBLE) on the output column: the Grafana plugin's converter map handles only BOOL/INT2/FLOAT4/FLOAT8/TIMESTAMP, so a DECIMAL column arrives as a string and the panel reports \"Data is missing a number field\". The inner sum stays DECIMAL, where the exactness matters."
